<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yuwen Yidougui</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 344</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yuwen Yidougui was the last chief of the Yuwen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xianbei">Xianbei</a>, a confederation in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaoning">Liaoning</a>. In 344 he was defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murong-huang">Murong Huang</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/former-yan">Former Yan</a>, fled into the steppe and died there, and his people were absorbed and resettled. Later rulers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-wei">Western Wei</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-zhou">Northern Zhou</a> claimed descent from the Yuwen.</p></div>
